  "title": "29 April 1964: The Beatles are photographed with their Madame Tussauds wax figures",
  "date": "1964-04-29",
  "content": "<div class=\"ast-post-format- single-layout-1\"><div class=\"entry-content clear\" itemprop=\"text\"><p>The London wax museum Madame Tussaud’s had unveiled effigies of all four Beatles on <a href=\"/1964/03/28/madame-tussauds-unveils-beatles-wax-figures/\">28 March 1964</a>. The Beatles were the first pop group to appear in the museum. <span id=\"more-30330\"></span></p><p>On 29 April the band were photographed with the dummies at the museum.</p><div data-carousel-extra=\"{&quot;blog_id&quot;:1,&quot;permalink&quot;:&quot;https://www.beatlesbible.com/1964/04/29/beatles-photographed-with-madame-tussauds-wax-figures/&quot;}\" id=\"gallery-1\" class=\"gallery galleryid-30330 gallery-columns-3 gallery-size-thumbnail\"><figure class=\"gallery-item\"><div class=\"gallery-icon landscape\">\n<a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/1964-photos/640429-beatles-madame-tussauds_01/\"><img decoding=\"sync\" width=\"200\" height=\"197\" src=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/640429-beatles-madame-tussauds_01-200x197.jpg\" class=\"attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail\" alt=\"The Beatles with their Madame Tussaud's waxwork figures, London, 29 April 1964\" srcset=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/640429-beatles-madame-tussauds_01-200x197.jpg 200w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/640429-beatles-madame-tussauds_01-580x570.jpg 580w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/640429-beatles-madame-tussauds_01-66x66.jpg 66w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/640429-beatles-madame-tussauds_01.jpg 600w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\" data-attachment-id=\"36972\" data-permalink=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/1964-photos/640429-beatles-madame-tussauds_01/\" data-orig-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/640429-beatles-madame-tussauds_01.jpg\" data-orig-size=\"600,590\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-title=\"The Beatles with their Madame Tussaud&amp;#8217;s waxwork figures, London, 29 April 1964\" data-image-description=\"\